@startuml
!theme plain
title Retry, DLQ and Human-Governed Redrive — Synthetic
autonumber
queue "Source Topic" as Source
participant "Status Consumer" as Consumer
database "Inbox / Error Store" as DB
queue "Retry Topic / Scheduler" as Retry
queue "Dead Letter Topic" as DLQ
actor "Operations" as Ops
participant "Provider Status Inquiry" as Provider
Source -> Consumer : Event to process
Consumer -> DB : Validate + transactional state work
alt Valid new event
 DB --> Consumer : COMMIT
 Consumer -> Source : Commit offset
else Temporary DB failure
 DB --> Consumer : Transient exception
 Consumer -> Retry : Durable controlled scheduling (if reordering acceptable)
 Retry --> Consumer : Retry with backoff + attempt counter
 note over Consumer,Retry
 Alternatively pause partition and retry in place
 to preserve ordering for a business key.
 end note
else Permanent invalid message
 DB --> Consumer : Schema validation failed
 Consumer -> DLQ : Durable quarantine with reason / metadata
 DLQ --> Consumer : Broker acknowledgement
 Consumer -> Source : Commit offset only after durable quarantine
 DLQ -> Ops : Incident / manual review
 Ops -> DB : Inspect correlation and current state
 opt Recovery requires provider authority
  Ops -> Provider : Query actual payment status
  Provider --> Ops : Authoritative result
 end
 Ops -> Retry : Approved corrected redrive with same business ID
 Retry --> Consumer : Reprocess with dedupe and state guard
end
@enduml